{%- comment -%}
  Hero event badge (seal sticker). Rendered hidden and empty: it shows only
  once PawScout's /public/event feed confirms something the calendar can
  vouch for (ONE fetch per page view, shared with the welcome offer and the
  announcement bar; the worker answers with Cache-Control max-age=120,
  measured 2026-11-14). theme.js paints it, then reveals it:
    - a running event: its name, then "<pct>% off with code <code>" (plus
      "until <end>" when it fits the seal); the seal hides again when the
      event's end time passes on an open page;
    - nothing running but a planned event: "Next: <name>" and its dates.
      Name and dates only: codes and percentages are never announced ahead;
    - every date and time is built from the feed's timestamps in the
      visitor's own time zone, never from the worker's prose labels;
    - nothing running and nothing planned, or the feed unreachable, slow or
      malformed: the seal stays hidden. Owner decision 2026-11-14 (PRD T20b):
      no copy of its own, so it can never show a stale stamp such as the
      summer one it carried until then.
  Every word a visitor reads comes from the feed. The seal is positioned
  absolutely (assets/theme.css) at every width, so revealing it late moves
  nothing. The emoji for the two states live here rather than in JS so a
  copy tweak never needs a script change. Sizes for feed copy are scoped
  below: event names and date ranges run longer than the two-word stamp the
  seal was drawn for.
{%- endcomment -%}
<a
  class="hero-event-badge"
  data-event-badge
  data-event-emoji-active="🎉"
  data-event-emoji-next="📅"
  href="{{ routes.all_products_collection_url }}"
  hidden
>
  <span class="hero-event-badge-emoji" aria-hidden="true"></span>
  <span class="hero-event-badge-title"></span>
  <span class="hero-event-badge-sub"></span>
</a>
{% style %}
  .hero-event-badge[hidden] { display: none; }
  .hero-event-badge[data-event-state] { gap: 4px; }
  .hero-event-badge[data-event-state] .hero-event-badge-emoji { font-size: 24px; }
  .hero-event-badge[data-event-state] .hero-event-badge-title {
    font-size: 13px;
    line-height: 1.12;
    letter-spacing: 0.01em;
    overflow-wrap: anywhere;
  }
  .hero-event-badge[data-event-state] .hero-event-badge-sub {
    max-width: 118px;
    font-size: 10.5px;
    line-height: 1.25;
  }
{% endstyle %}
